pe":{"trend_h5":0.086,"trend_h21":-0.0356,"reversal_h5":-0.2739,"reversal_h21":-0.1021,"ar1_h21":-0.1969,"har_h5_scaled":0.4159},"slope_boot_p":{"trend_h5":0.171,"trend_h21":0.996,"reversal_h5":0.963,"reversal_h21":0.66,"ar1_h21":0.928}},{"period":"Unseen months 2025-07..2026-09 (reported)","months":15,"slope":{"trend_h5":-0.1368,"trend_h21":-0.0222,"reversal_h5":-0.0359,"reversal_h21":-0.1607,"ar1_h21":-0.0815,"har_h5_scaled":-1.2194},"slope_boot_p":{"trend_h5":0.703,"trend_h21":0.886,"reversal_h5":0.728,"reversal_h21":0.592,"ar1_h21":0.562}}]},{"id":"a2","title":"Co-moving groups against matched random baskets (2008–2019)","x_label":"Forecaster","y_label":"Out-of-sample R² (%)","note":"Matched baskets: one non-member per member from the same 5x5 cell of beta and volatility, 20 replicates each with its own fit. Pass needed Holm-corrected p < 0.05 among the plan's secondaries. signflip_null_gap: the groups-minus-matched gap when every real relation is destroyed (200 draws, added after results as a reading aid).","forecasters":[{"forecaster":"Trend, 5 days","groups_r2_pct":-0.9045,"matched_r2_pct":-1.322,"diff_pct":0.4175,"diff_ci90_pct":[-0.5508,1.6357],"boot_p":0.2663,"holm_within_a2":0.5325,"signflip_null_gap":{"null_mean_pct":0.272,"null_sd_pct":0.329,"share_null_ge_observed":0.265}},{"forecaster":"Trend, 21 days","groups_r2_pct":-1.2311,"matched_r2_pct":-2.5412,"diff_pct":1.3101,"diff_ci90_pct":[0.2298,2.6264],"boot_p":0.0168,"holm_within_a2":0.084,"signflip_null_gap":{"null_mean_pct":0.545,"null_sd_pct":0.488,"share_null_ge_observed":0.065}},{"forecaster":"Reversal, 5 days","groups_r2_pct":-1.4752,"matched_r2_pct":-2.4039,"diff_pct":0.9287,"diff_ci90_pct":[-0.1063,1.9666],"boot_p":0.0707,"holm_within_a2":0.2828,"signflip_null_gap":{"null_mean_pct":0.7,"null_sd_pct":0.364,"share_null_ge_observed":0.22}},{"forecaster":"Reversal, 21 days","groups_r2_pct":-0.4673,"matched_r2_pct":-1.341,"diff_pct":0.8737,"diff_ci90_pct":[-0.5341,2.3392],"boot_p":0.1662,"holm_within_a2":0.4986,"signflip_null_gap":{"null_mean_pct":0.516,"null_sd_pct":0.403,"share_null_ge_observed":0.13}},{"forecaster":"Last-month return (AR(1)), 21 days","groups_r2_pct":-0.3373,"matched_r2_pct":-0.4288,"diff_pct":0.0915,"diff_ci90_pct":[-0.2556,0.4471],"boot_p":0.3239,"holm_within_a2":0.5325,"signflip_null_gap":{"null_mean_pct":0.291,"null_sd_pct":0.27,"share_null_ge_observed":0.85}}]}],"can_and_cant_show":["A1 asked whether time-varying predictability rises with aggregation, against the historical mean and not only against zero. Not shown: against the historical mean no level was forecastable by these signals, so there was nothing for aggregation to raise.","It cannot show that aggregates are unforecastable: only that three plain price signals, calibrated by one straight line per level, did not forecast them. Many-characteristic forecasts (as in Gu, Kelly & Xiu 2020) were not tested.","The test as written has little power: the volatility control rose from 4.1% at single stocks to 7.4% at 100-stock baskets and the market's Clark-West t was 3.2, yet its slope p was 0.25. The market rung is one series of 144 months, the fitting penalty grows up the ladder, and the bar is t >= 3. A small real effect could hide; a large one would not have produced negative R² everywhere.","Against zero, aggregates look forecastable when they are not: SPY scores +2.7% to +4.2% against zero but -1.5% to +0.1% against its own average. That is the drift the plan warned about.","A2 asked whether economically linked groups add predictability beyond matched random baskets. Not shown: groups lose less than matched baskets for all five forecasters, but both are below zero, and with every real relation destroyed the gap is already +0.3 to +0.7 points, because groups' signals are more spread out and their fitted line less noisy.","2008–2009 was the worst period for every forecaster and the largest A2 gap; the price data holds only surviving companies, so crisis results may be biased.","The 16 unseen months (15 decision months) agree but confirm nothing: about 65 earlier experiments have read them.","Nothing here bears on the curvature half of the idea (B), and no result shows any law, relativistic or otherwise, governing markets."],"provenance":{"results_file":"research/market_geometry/results_A.md","plan":"experiments/untested-luca-market-geometry.md","data":"Stooq prices through 2025-06-27 (judge export fingerprint 8b5ac076267c83ab); unseen months from the 2026-10-19 export (5e2aaa6254c435e6)","units":"R² and slopes in percentage points of R²; slopes per unit of natural-log basket size (1 stock to the market = 7.16 units)","forward_test":"pending (no git tag yet)"}}